WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
- You know some stuff about
me that's pretty dark.

00:00:01.510 --> 00:00:03.012
I know some stuff about
you that's pretty weird.

00:00:03.012 --> 00:00:04.125
I mean a lot of the stuff we know is

00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:05.443
probably not TV friendly.

00:00:05.443 --> 00:00:07.134
(laughs)

00:00:07.134 --> 00:00:09.090
(bouncing music)

00:00:11.771 --> 00:00:13.910
- [Mathew] I don't know if I
wrote it big enough, though.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:14.862
- [Thomas] We'll find out. Ready?

00:00:14.862 --> 00:00:16.244
- [Mathew] You want to show it now?

00:00:16.244 --> 00:00:17.077
- My answer is

00:00:18.137 --> 00:00:19.629
"Stretching out like Richard Simmons".

00:00:22.927 --> 00:00:24.730
- [Mathew] I misspelled something.

00:00:25.671 --> 00:00:27.451
- Smoking and/or lounging.

00:00:27.451 --> 00:00:29.399
- Lying on a couch.

00:00:29.399 --> 00:00:30.730
We do know each other!

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:31.184
- We know each other very well.

00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.185
- Fudge!

00:00:41.185 --> 00:00:41.914
What do we got?

00:00:41.914 --> 00:00:42.878
- Fuck.

00:00:42.878 --> 00:00:45.164
- Oh! Yeah! I had the
upbeat version of that.

00:00:47.544 --> 00:00:48.657
- [Thomas] I think it's fun.

00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:50.251
You got that sort of a Canadian flare.

00:00:50.251 --> 00:00:51.922
Is it "clusterfuck"?

00:00:53.912 --> 00:00:56.210
Like, "This has turned into
a real clusterfuck, eh?"

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.185
- No, that's not a swear word.

00:00:58.185 --> 00:00:58.849
- What do you got?

00:00:58.849 --> 00:00:59.607
- Fuck face.

00:00:59.607 --> 00:01:01.208
- Oh, fuck face. I was close.

00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:03.483
- "Clusterfuck" you thought
was my favorite swear word?

00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:05.097
- I don't know. I was just
trying to think of a word.

00:01:05.097 --> 00:01:06.707
I don't hear you swear very much.

00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:07.499
- I swear a lot.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:08.031
- Really?

00:01:08.031 --> 00:01:08.512
- Yeah.

00:01:08.512 --> 00:01:09.183
- Not at me.

00:01:09.183 --> 00:01:09.797
- No, internally.

00:01:09.797 --> 00:01:10.140
- No.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.027
- [Mathew] You should hear
what I'm saying right now.

00:01:18.626 --> 00:01:19.605
- What is it?

00:01:19.605 --> 00:01:21.548
- [Woman Offscreen] Yoga and juggling.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:22.597
- Yeah, very different.

00:01:22.597 --> 00:01:25.767
If you think I'm good at yoga,
you should see me juggle.

00:01:25.767 --> 00:01:27.270
[Thomas] Look how quickly
I started writing.

00:01:28.191 --> 00:01:30.591
- [Mathew] I don't know
what my secret talent is.

00:01:30.591 --> 00:01:31.376
- Want me to tell you?

00:01:33.076 --> 00:01:34.566
(laughs)

00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:37.465
Show yours first.

00:01:37.465 --> 00:01:39.486
Complaining.

00:01:39.486 --> 00:01:40.786
Or tennis.

00:01:44.099 --> 00:01:45.571
[Thomas] I really was one.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:47.192
It's "Not Most Likely to Have Jazz Hands".

00:01:47.192 --> 00:01:48.093
What'd you put?

00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:51.425
No, I was voted "Most Likely to Succeed".

00:01:51.425 --> 00:01:52.262
- You were?

00:01:52.262 --> 00:01:53.521
- I was.

00:01:53.521 --> 00:01:55.786
- I was voted "Most Talkative".

00:01:55.786 --> 00:01:57.425
- There you go. I could see that.

00:01:59.048 --> 00:02:00.487
[Mathew] You're writing
much longer than I am.

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:01.744
[Thomas] Well I drew a little
picture to your reaction

00:02:01.744 --> 00:02:02.629
to the thing, too.

00:02:02.629 --> 00:02:04.079
What did you write?

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:05.169
- Well, I can't tell you.

00:02:05.169 --> 00:02:06.613
- I wrote green things.

00:02:06.613 --> 00:02:07.616
- I wrote fish.

00:02:09.356 --> 00:02:10.494
- I forgot you hate fish.

00:02:10.494 --> 00:02:11.138
- I hate fish.

00:02:12.061 --> 00:02:13.473
- I know that for a while I was buying you

00:02:13.473 --> 00:02:14.989
a green juice every day and then

00:02:14.989 --> 00:02:16.294
one day you said "Don't
ever do that again".

00:02:16.294 --> 00:02:17.259
- Yeah, that's true.

00:02:23.371 --> 00:02:24.397
- I honestly can't think of anything.

00:02:24.397 --> 00:02:26.385
I can't think of anything.

00:02:26.385 --> 00:02:27.119
- Look what I wrote.

00:02:27.119 --> 00:02:29.449
- I know. I'm just a positive person.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.168
[Thomas] Come on.

00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:31.168
[Mathew] Oh.

00:02:32.224 --> 00:02:34.117
[Thomas] Uh oh, did we stumble?

00:02:34.117 --> 00:02:35.469
I'm gonna hold mine up over here.

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:39.989
[Women Offscreen] Now see. Let's review.

00:02:40.841 --> 00:02:42.209
- Hazel. Very close.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:43.926
- I'm close and you're right.

00:02:43.926 --> 00:02:44.524
- Yeah.

00:02:46.574 --> 00:02:48.344
- This is going to sound
sort of tacky and small time,

00:02:48.344 --> 00:02:50.042
but can we keep the markers?

00:02:50.931 --> 00:02:51.885
- This is a great marker.

00:02:51.885 --> 00:02:55.040
- Amazing markers! Amazing markers!

